   "reading": "the last way takes half the time of the first, and what it has over the third is the parts apart and nothing else. Why that is worth what it is is not known: the compiled code takes one number at a time, with not one instruction that takes two. The window and the overlap-add in one pass are within what two runs of one kernel differ by, and were not taken"
  },
